    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I used AI tools like ChatGPT to check my algebra homework. It helped me understand steps I missed, but I noticed it sometimes gave overly complex solutions. I’d recommend using it for quick checks, not as a replacement for practice.",
    "How would you explain, step by step, how to solve a second order algebraic equation?": "First, write the equation in standard form: ax² + bx + c = 0. Then, calculate the discriminant (b² - 4ac). If it’s positive, you get two real solutions; zero, one solution; negative, complex numbers. Finally, use the quadratic formula: x = [-b ± √(discriminant)] / (2a).",
